  "description": "Q12 frozen blind compatibility pair list. No labels. Labels are sealed in compatibility_2026_q12_labels_hidden.json and were assigned before any prediction was run.",
  "selection_policy": "36 pairs, of which 24 form 12 CONTRAST GROUPS: two pairs sharing one material whose correct answers are OPPOSITE (e.g. PVDF+NMP soluble vs PP+NMP insoluble). Q11 showed a constant fallback score can pass a set dominated by 'incompatible' labels by base rate alone; a contrast group cannot be passed that way, because any constant scores both members identically and must get one wrong. Zero material-name-pair overlap against blind_test_pairs, ground_truth, all prior external_blind (Q2-Q11), and all dev_compatibility. All names resolve in a bridge vocabulary.",
  "holdout_policy": "Q12 is current_blind and UNSCORED. Run for reporting only. Never use for tuning or calibration. If its errors are inspected for remediation it becomes spent_diagnostic and a new blind set must be frozen. Q10 remains separately sealed.",
  "known_limitations": [
    "Labels are expert judgment from materials-science first principles, not curated external experimental ground truth.",
    "Labels were authored by the same AI assistant that has worked on this codebase; weaker independence than an external labeler, disclosed deliberately.",
    "Pairs reuse known materials in unused combinations; this does not test out-of-vocabulary materials.",
    "Borderline pairs are flagged in the sealed label file and should be reported separately from clear-cut ones."
  ],
